      "source_text": "During a dust storm on 18 October 2025, solar output fell by thirty-four percent in fifteen minutes. Battery-cabinet temperature rose by eight degrees Celsius, and the inverter fan developed an unusual low- frequency vibration The controller did not shut down the entire station It disconnected secondary heaters, reduced selected lighting. started the backup generator, and issued a maintenance warning Diagnostic software identified three plausible faults debris covering part of the solar array, wear in a fan bearing, and increasing contact resistance at a battery connector These possibilities were ranked, but none was presented as certain because the measurements could be explained by more than one physical condition",
